# ONE CONCEPT: a `dyn` parameter is CALL-BY-NEED. methodParameters writes `_x: => T` (a default rides along,
# `_start: => Int = 0`); methodBody opens with a PRELUDE `lazy val x: T = _x` per lazy parameter, so the
# body reads the bare name and evaluates it at most once — the factory convention (`_name` -> `lazy val
# name`) applied to methods. A method with a prelude is always a block. Abstract methods carry the same
# signature (Presence.fold), so implementers match. `now` on a parameter keeps `x: T` and no prelude.
